# stream-dvr build environment. Copy to .env and uncomment what you need.
# Contributors: update internal/buildenv/*.go and run `make generate`.
#
# ///////////////////////////////////////////////
# stream-dvr Build Environment
# ///////////////////////////////////////////////
#
# The Makefile reads .env when it exists, so a value set there reaches
# every build without being typed. .env is not committed and this template
# is, which is why every line below is commented out and holds no value.

# ///// VERSION /////

# The version the binary reports. Taken from the nearest git tag when
# unset, which is what a release build wants.
#
# Unset: the version is derived from git, or reads 0.0.0-dev with the
# commit when there is no tag.
#VERSION=1.2.3

# ///// REPO_OWNER /////

# The GitHub account this project is published under. It builds the links
# the binary points back at: issues, raw content, update checks.
#
# Unset: read from the git remote, and empty before the repository is
# published.
#REPO_OWNER=example-owner

# ///// REPO_NAME /////

# The GitHub repository name, alongside REPO_OWNER.
#
# Unset: read from the git remote, and empty before the repository is
# published.
#REPO_NAME=example-repo
